  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n# Correct state\r\n\r\nWhen I use the button to trigger the dialog's showModal method, there is no black border and the effect is rendered correctly\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"en\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    <title>Document</title>\r\n    <style>\r\n        dialog{\r\n            border: 0px ;\r\n            background-color: white;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n    <button>打开</button>\r\n    <dialog @click=\"handleClickOutside\">\r\n        <div class=\"ru-dialog-content\" @click.stop>\r\n            <slot></slot>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </dialog>\r\n\r\n    <script>\r\n        const dia =  document.querySelector(\"dialog\")\r\n        document.querySelector(\"button\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\r\n            dia.showModal();\r\n        })\r\n\r\n    </script>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\nThe render effect is shown below：\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f1fbfb76-1d21-4806-85d8-6c64f7f91a8b)\r\n\r\n# A bug exists\r\n\r\nWhen I trigger a showModal with a label other than button (e.g. div, p), it causes the dialog to appear with a black border that cannot be removed\r\n\r\n```html\r\n\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"en\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    <title>Document</title>\r\n    <style>\r\n        dialog{\r\n            border: 0px ;\r\n            background-color: white;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n    <div>打开</div>\r\n    <dialog @click=\"handleClickOutside\">\r\n        <div class=\"ru-dialog-content\" @click.stop>\r\n            <slot></slot>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </dialog>\r\n\r\n    <script>\r\n        const dia =  document.querySelector(\"dialog\")\r\n        document.querySelector(\"div\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\r\n            dia.showModal();\r\n        })\r\n\r\n    </script>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe effect is as follows：\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5ec40564-ed69-4544-a9f4-5dac7d4c3560)\r\n\r\n",
